心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:06.020
Episode Twenty-One: 
Invisible Wall

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.180
B-1, C-1, no problems.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:16.310
Okay.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:18.590
C-2, C-3...

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:20.790
Should we switch?

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:22.500
What? Lucky us!

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.330
Bzzt!

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.680
This is the result of a fair game of rock, paper, scissors.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:29.520
Shipon, be sure not to miss the 0.1 micron scratches!

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.870
The area around the thrusters is easily magnetized...

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.260
...so be careful when you polish it.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.310
Jojo.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.520
So how far have you gone?

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.030
With what?

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:45.410
Oh, playing dumb, are you?

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.450
We're asking you how far you've gotten with Akira.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:52.510
I-Is that the only thing inside your heads?

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.250
Oh, now he's pretending to be serious.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.110
In other words, in your own way, you've made progress.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:59.920
D-Don't get any closer, you perverts!

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:08.180
Shima-chan.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:11.770
What is it?

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:13.940
You're not avoiding me, are you?

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:15.730
I'm not avoiding you.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.000
You are avoiding me.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.000
That's not true. I'm talking to you right now, right?

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.220
What are those two doing?

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:29.550
They're fighting, aren't they?

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:30.590
Fighting?! 
 Fighting?!

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:32.330
Since when?

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:34.300
You hadn't realized?

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:35.450
Not at all.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.070
This is why...

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.750
Boys are...

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.260
Too slow-witted.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.250
They're no good at all!

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:43.430
- We're sorry. - We're sorry.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.080
One jumbo pizza!

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:49.400
I wonder if it's possible to get those two to make up...

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.600
It looked pretty bad, actually...

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.790
We say that, but what should we do?

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:00.780
I think it would have the reverse effect if we interfered too much.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:04.880
Even if you say that, it looks like nothing has changed recently.

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:08.330
It probably won't work, but shall we try to persuade them?

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:09.650
That's it.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:13.450
I agree. I don't like it when Shipon's depressed.

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:16.170
Wait, where are you going?

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:17.820
To where Shipon is.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:20.620
Hold on a second there, you little dynamite girl.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.530
That's right. We have to make sure to come up with a strategy.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.060
A strategy?

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:27.650
All right, this is it!

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.580
The decisive great make-up strategy!

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.670
That's too decisive.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:39.420
"The course of true love never did run true."

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.640
From "A Midsummer Night's Dream."

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:47.830
Now, what is on the other side of that course?

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:53.700
I'm used to standing while I talk.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.070
More importantly, I want to see it quickly.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:57.180
Yes, sir.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:01.830
We believe that the Cosmic Fracture's form is maintained...

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.530
...by releasing an enormous amount of energy...

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:10.650
...in the form of light, heat, electro- magnetic waves, gravity, and more.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:13.310
In other words, it's unusually unstable.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.680
If the amount of energy released is reduced...

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:18.290
...then it might close the tear for a moment.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.560
This is a simulation of the collapse of the Ultima from the other day.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:28.080
To counterbalance the energy released from the black hole...

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:33.030
...the fracture expended energy and lost kinetic energy.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.630
It can be assumed that the speed of its advance was reduced as a result.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.220
In other words, you're saying there was an exchange of energy...

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.390
...between the Fracture and the black hole?

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:42.170
That's correct.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:46.070
And if we could introduce an even greater amount of energy...

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:49.800
...then the Fracture would release energy to counterbalance it...

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:54.980
And become unable to maintain its form.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:56.650
Exactly.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.110
It looks like we might be able to do something.

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:02.170
But there are two problems.

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:14.410
Let's stop here for today.

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:18.540
Are you feeling bad?

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.090
Your blood pressure and your body temperature are both low.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.260
Your brain waves aren't stable.

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:24.700
It's nothing...

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:27.480
Then are you worried or something?

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.370
I'm not getting enough sleep, so I can't concentrate.

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.110
Not enough sleep, huh?

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:35.110
You know, you really can talk to me about it.

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:36.670
I'm all right.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:38.840
I'll get it right next time.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.360
What? How cold of you.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.070
Is it a worry you can't even talk to me about?

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:46.710
It really is nothing.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.470
I'm sorry about this.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.300
Kouta Otoyama.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:00.700
What?

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:02.410
Now, now, now, now, now...

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:04.660
We are best friends.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:06.570
And once in a while, fellow men.

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:08.470
Let's be completely open and talk!

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:10.140
W-What's going on?

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.450
So what's going on?

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:21.320
Not "what's going on?"

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:25.220
Kouta, isn't there something you want to talk to us about?

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:25.630
What?

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:29.050
You know, about you arguing with a certain someone or something?

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:29.680
Oh...

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:31.820
You're pretty gloomy all of the sudden...

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:35.660
Now, now! You might feel better if you let it all out at once.

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:36.500
Right...

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.030
Aren't they being too frank?

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:43.340
I wonder if it was a mistake to leave it to those three.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:45.320
Jojo.

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:48.550
You're going out with Kayama right now, right?

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.250
What? Yeah! What about that?

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:52.520
Suppose that...

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:55.910
Suppose that for some reason you don't understand...

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.500
...Kayama got angry at you all of the sudden.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:58.880
What would you do?

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:01.920
That's a pretty definite "suppose."

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:02.720
Shut up.

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:05.530
Well?

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:07.730
I'd apologize. 
 What?

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:11.460
In any case, I'd apologize until she gave in.

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:12.790
I'd do that first.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:16.410
But you don't even know why she's angry.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:18.810
What'll happen if you split hairs over it?

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:20.570
You want to make up, right?

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:22.600
Well, yes, but...

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:25.660
Women are creatures of emotion.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:29.280
In any case, if you think things are bad, or even if you're right...

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:32.340
...you have to apologize, apologize, apologize until she gives in.

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:35.720
That's not logical.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:41.280
I'm telling you, logic doesn't work on girls.

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:47.940
Love begins when you forget words like "justice" or "reality."

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:49.030
Huh?

00:08:57.580 --> 00:09:01.460
So even if you think you're right, you'll apologize first...

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:02.670
No...

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:06.520
Maybe I should call that a figure of speech or...

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:07.240
Figure of speech?

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:09.010
Don't underestimate women!

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:15.230
You saw, right? Logic doesn't work with them.

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:18.320
Yeah...

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:20.000
That's right...

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:26.370
l-lt's a misunderstanding, Akira!!!

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:29.830
I really understand how difficult it is now.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.610
This is a simulation of the fluctuations in the energy...

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:34.880
...that the Cosmic Fracture emits.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.790
It displays the individual radiation intensity for each wave...

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:42.020
Electromagnetic, heat, gravity waves, neutrinos, and others.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:44.490
In order to close the Fracture it is necessary to hit it...

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:45.930
...with an enormous amount of energy at just the right place.

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:52.900
In other words, where all of the energy discharges are at their lowest.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:58.310
The greatest problem is that the target keeps changing, just like this.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.780
And actually, it's much more complicated...

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.540
...and it's nearly impossible to predict or observe.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.180
And the other problem is?

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.560
The total amount of energy that needs to be emitted.

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:12.740
The amount of energy needed for the Great Wall can only be created...

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:17.310
...by a Foundation-class space station, right?

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:21.160
Yes. But because the target point is normally changing...

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:25.670
...it would have to be closer than even the Ultima was when it collapsed.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:29.470
But if something that has the great mass of a Foundation...

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:32.950
...gets too close to the Fracture, then this would happen.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.760
A craft with a small mass, you say?

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:54.490
Are you saying we're going to use the Infinity?

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:55.420
That's right.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.860
The Foundations can't get close to the Fracture...

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:00.970
...but they can emit the necessary energy.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.750
The lasers that are emitted will converge via gravity control.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:12.510
The Infinity will allow them to be concentrated in one point...

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:14.640
...and shoot the target on the Fracture.

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.020
The problem is the pilot.

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:20.870
With the new DLS only being usable by Kouta Otoyama...

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:24.600
Will Shima Katase be all right as his assistant?

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:26.040
Certainly...

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:29.480
There IS the matter of what happened the other day, after all...

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.420
Is it decided that Otoyama will be the pilot?

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:36.710
Perhaps we could look at the regular students or others above them again.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:39.630
That might be a little too leisurely for a point in time...

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.220
...when humanity might be destroyed.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:43.940
I understand how you feel...

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:47.090
...but thinking about it calmly might be the correct action as well.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.350
Otoyama's appointment is definite.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:53.050
In which case...

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:56.550
Don't we need to consider who is the most competent person...

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.530
...to be his assistant?

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:19.050
Kouta...

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:22.200
Oh, Machida-sempai.

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:24.040
I'm sorry.

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:25.250
It's all right.

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:30.530
So what happened with those two?

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:33.800
Right after, I saw them walking together happily.

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:37.700
Kayama looked so happy as she held Jojo's hand...

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:41.050
...and Jojo still had the slap mark on his cheek.

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:43.680
I don't understand at all.

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:48.280
It's the springtime of their life... It's so nice.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:49.240
Huh?

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:53.280
Fighting over stupid things and making up...

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:55.570
Aren't things like that fun?

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:58.020
Is that what kind of things those are?

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:01.020
Well...

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:05.020
I was focused on my studies...

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:08.800
...so I kind of yearned for those kinds of things.

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:11.160
I don't understand at all.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:14.540
I think it would be better to not fight.

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:16.840
You're serious-minded, aren't you?

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:19.770
That doesn't sound like you're complimenting me.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.340
Sorry, sorry.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:36.600
Jeez, what are you guys doing?

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:38.250
Sorry... 
Sorry...

00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:42.330
But now we know that Kouta wants to make up, right?

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:47.240
So isn't the problem that Shipon won't talk to Kouta?

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:49.590
What? Are you saying Shipon's at fault?

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:51.930
No, that's not it, but...

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:53.340
All right, I understand.

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:56.780
Let's go with drastic measures!

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:59.610
Drastic measures!

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:02.660
All right, we're going to be successful this time!

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:06.100
Hmm?

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:10.330
What the...?

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:12.360
Just when I thought you'd gotten back on your feet...

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:13.880
...you're feeling down again?

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:15.960
Kind of...

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:21.190
Hey, as teachers, what are we supposed to do for our students?

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.740
Huh? Why are you asking that now, of all times?

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.140
Because it is now.

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:30.440
Did the genius boy and the others get another tough job or something?

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:31.280
Yeah.

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:33.910
And this time it's not just the fate of the Earth...

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.400
The fate of the entire solar system is on the line.

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:40.070
That's not what's bothering you though, right?

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.620
Well, no.

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:45.830
What's with me... just readily sending those two off on missions?

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:48.890
Saying it's because they're competent...

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:51.900
...or because they're the only ones who can do it...

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:56.530
But they're the ones who can do it best, right?

00:14:58.180 --> 00:15:02.970
What I want to ask is, as a teacher, am I all right with doing that?

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:07.230
I can only say something cliched...

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.740
...but maybe all we can do is what we're able to.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:13.850
Even if that's just to watch over the students.

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.340
That really was cliched.

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:19.460
Sorry.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:22.430
All right!

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:28.600
Brooding doesn't suit me. I'm going to do what I'm able to.

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:30.360
Good, do that.

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:31.920
Thanks.

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:33.080
Sure.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:35.300
All right!

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:48.980
What's wrong? Why are you all spaced out?

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:50.980
No reason.

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:55.110
So everyone's tired, huh?

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:56.730
What do you mean by that?

00:15:57.400 --> 00:15:59.420
Otoyama, the preparatory student.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:01.730
What about Kouta Otoyama?

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:05.440
He's completely preoccupied with a girl.

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:08.100
He's so out of it, the poor guy.

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:10.750
It's kind of cute too, though.

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:12.520
Shima Katase, huh?

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.180
Girls like that are better at getting the attention of boys...

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:19.050
...than sexy women like you, Ren, you know?

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:23.480
Oh, you said it. There was a guy like that in our class, Shane Simmons.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:28.890
Right. Those types of guys are oblivious, so they're hard to deal with.

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:32.900
Does that mean the world hasn't changed very much?

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:34.580
Neither have we.

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:41.930
You might be right.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:45.980
Shipon.

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:53.190
What in the world do you want?

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:04.310
I'm sorry, Shipon, but when you two fight, it's tough on us, too.

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:05.830
So we thought about a lot of different things...

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:08.970
But we think it's good if you two meet and say what you want to say once.

00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:10.530
We think if you do, you'll feel relieved.

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:12.700
We'll be waiting outside, okay?

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:23.050
Hey...

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:24.790
What is it?

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:28.180
Do you hate me now?

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:29.470
I don't hate you.

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:32.660
I don't hate you, but...

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:37.390
I might have stopped liking you.

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:38.840
What's that supposed to mean?

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:42.940
The new DLS. 
 What?

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:46.710
You're the only one who can use it, right, Kouta?

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:50.890
Right now... it's still tuned to my specifications...

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:54.890
But I think other people who can use it will appear in time.

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:58.330
But that probably won't be me, right?

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.480
We don't know that.

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:01.390
That's not it.

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:05.840
I mean, I can't even use the normal DLS that well.

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:09.200
Wait a second! What are you talking about?

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:15.040
I can't see the things you can see, Kouta!

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:17.090
Shima-chan?

00:18:17.810 --> 00:18:18.680
Kouta, you're...

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:22.100
You're different from me!

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:24.900
Shipon!

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:28.250
Wait, Shima-chan!

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:30.880
What did you say to Shipon?

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:32.680
I don't know...

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:35.830
Not at all...

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:39.300
I just don't understand at all...

00:18:41.530 --> 00:18:45.200
Wah, that was a huge failure!

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:49.340
Maybe it would have been better to plan out our strategy more.

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:51.740
It's because you guys are completely useless...

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:54.340
...that we went with a plan to get them together directly.

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:56.150
We're sorry.
 We're sorry.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.880
One jumbo doria.

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:02.000
At first, those two were getting along so well...

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:03.880
So what in the world caused them to fight?

00:19:04.570 --> 00:19:07.760
Because Shipon stopped being able to keep up with Kouta?

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:09.030
It couldn't be!

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:13.090
Maybe Kouta tried to force himself on Shipon?

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:16.750
He isn't like someone else we know.

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:18.990
Did you try to force yourself on her, man?

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:20.680
I didn't, I'm telling you.

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:22.680
Rather, I attempted to.

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:24.120
You beast!

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:27.970
In other words, Kouta's the one at fault?

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:30.040
That's not it.

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:33.280
Then Shipon has someone else she likes now or something?

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:34.620
There's no way that would happen!

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:36.440
Then what is it?

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:38.670
And this is why... 
Boys are...

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:40.490
They're just no good at all, right?

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:42.390
We heard that before, too.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.130
We're just making sure.

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:47.230
Space Academy preparatory student Shima Katase...

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:50.260
Space Academy preparatory student Shima Katase...

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:53.530
...please go to the headmaster's office right away.

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:55.100
She's being called?

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:58.100
I wonder if Shipon's turned off her cell phone.

00:19:58.620 --> 00:19:59.950
This is serious...

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:04.720
Regarding the mysterious lights seen in southern skies recently...

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:06.220
...the Sol System Alliance...

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:08.680
...along with the International Astronomical Society...

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:11.570
...have announced that they have confirmed its true nature.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:15.160
This astronomical body has been named the Cosmic Fracture...

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:17.560
A tear in space.

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:21.640
In terms of a response to the Fracture that is closing in on the Sol System...

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:25.460
...the Sol System Alliance will announce the collective views...

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:28.440
...of all of the Foundations within a few days.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:31.300
Shima Katase, reporting.

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:41.970
Shima Katase. 
Yes, sir.

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:44.310
Kouta Otoyama.

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:45.120
Yes, sir.

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:48.440
I want you to listen carefully to what I'm going to say from here on...

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:55.090
For as long as I am able, I will supply you with materials.

00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:57.330
Thank you very much.

00:20:58.140 --> 00:21:01.830
It's certainly true that the greatest problem has yet to be solved.

00:21:02.550 --> 00:21:06.260
But all we can do is move forward, one step at a time.

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:08.140
Isn't that right? 
 Yes.

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:17.820
For better or for worse, one step at a time.

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:36.390
Humanity will grow more spiritual. I want to believe that.

00:21:40.710 --> 00:21:46.450
Humanity needs time. Time to grow.

